# Code owners: the reviewers GitHub requests on a pull request. The maintainer
# reviews every path; the platform team joins on release files, repository
# automation, licence and security texts. Paths are root-anchored and the last
# matching line wins, so a path line names every owner it needs.

# Every path
*                                   @hervenivon

# Release version and changelog files
/CHANGELOG.md                       @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/.release-please-manifest.json      @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/addons/scenario/plugin.cfg         @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform

# Release machinery and repository automation
/release-please-config.json         @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/.github/workflows/                 @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/.github/actions/                   @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/.github/dependabot.yml             @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/tools/toolkit.py                   @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform

# Licence and security texts
/LICENSE                            @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/addons/scenario/LICENSE            @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
/SECURITY.md                        @hervenivon @scenario-labs/platform
